// OPEN — aug18a class 4 (katana divergence_000000). Mechanism located,
// fix is emission surgery awaiting design sign-off.
//
//   interp: Trace([1:i64:2 2:i64:0 3:i64:2])   (canonical)
//   jit:    Trace([1:i64:2 2:i64:0 3:i64:4])
//
// x iterates 2,0,2. On the shrink to 0 the interp DELETES the slots
// (collection.rs slot.delete) so the regrow builds fresh `count`
// state (1+1=2); the kernel's per-slot site-chain state survives and
// the counts continue (2+2=4). The negative-size face in the soak
// finding is a red herring — plain 0 reproduces.
//
// Root cause: every slot-chain ensure/truncate (`graphix_slot_state_
// table`/`_blocks`) for IN-LOOP call sites and DynCall cache pairs is
// emitted per-iteration INSIDE the loop body (emit_site_block,
// claim_slot_cache_words) — a zero-length loop never runs them, so a
// shrink-to-zero never truncates and the regrow sees no length
// change. Guarded-select tables don't have this hole at their own
// level (open_slot_tables ensures them in the always-executed
// preheader), but nested levels do (an OUTER len-0 epoch skips the
// inner preheader entirely).
//
// Fix direction (needs Eric): every loop level that a chain threads
// must run that level's ensure whenever the level's preheader runs —
// i.e. claims made during body emission need their partial chains
// emitted into each enclosing loop's always-executed block. Cranelift
// forbids out-of-order block filling (switch_to_block asserts the
// current block is filled), so the mechanism is a PREWALK: extend the
// guarded_select_sites prewalk to enumerate in-loop DynCall sites and
// callee call sites, pre-claim their anchors in open_slot_tables, and
// have body emission look the claims up (exactly how select sites
// already work). Fallback for prewalk misses: claim-at-emission as
// today, plus a debug assert to catch drift.
{let x = array::iter([i64:2, i64:0, i64:2]); array::fold(array::init(x, |i| i), i64:0, |acc, e| acc + count(e))}
